XMISCELLANEOUS SPOILERS:
X
XHere are a few odds and ends that I have discovered over many games.
X
XPotions
X
XI always drink unidentified potions immediately. Rarely will they
Xcause irreparable damage, and there's no sense in filling up your
Xpack with useless ones. After identifying 'gain level' I save up
Xthese until I have enough to reach the ^T autoteleport experience
Xlevel. Whenever possible, I keep an 'extra healing' around until
XI find 'hallucination', and 'restore strength' until I identify
X'sickness'.
X
XRings
X
XTeleport and polymorph control are the only two you need to
Xfinish the game. Most of the others will get you 'over the
Xhump' until you gain the appropriate intrinsic ability. Don't
Xtry on unidentified rings unless you're truly desperate.
X
XWands
X
XSomeone recently posted a spoiler for identifying every type of
Xwand without a scroll of identify. Wands are usually useful, but
Xnot necessary. If you want to really beat nethack into the ground,
Xand you have a polymorph wand, you can polymorph a pile of wands
Xuntil you get a wand of wishing, wish for more wands, and repeat
Xthe process to get as many wands of wishing as you want.
X
XArmor
X
XGood armor is really the secret to success. You want to keep
Xupgrading your armor throughout the game. Always replace a
X'weaker' class with a 'stronger' class, starting with splint,
Xthen banded, then bronze, then plate, and crystal plate. Elven
Xcloaks are a must. Carry an extra, if possible. Elven chain
Xmail is a good compromise, if you can't find any plate armor to
Xwear under a cloak. Be sure to collect one each of shields,
Xhelmets, and gloves. Rings of protection are another way to
Xsupplement your armor class. By the time you get your AC down
Xto -10, not much can hurt you!
X
XSpellbooks
X
XA rule of thumb is not to engrave spellbooks until you reach
Xexperience level 10 and identify the scroll of amnesia. If
Xyou dip your spellbooks in holy water before engraving, your
Xchances of successfully adding the spell are improved.
X
XShops
X
XShops are the treasure trove of nethack. Everything in a shop
Xis yours for the taking, once you know how. The strategy for
Xstealing can get involved, so let me offer just a few pointers.
XWhen you discover a new shop, move everthing worth taking into
Xa single pile before you gain intrinsic teleport ability. Kill
Xthe Mimics (if you can, that is) before you start picking things
Xup. When you are ready to do some shoplifting, be sure to leave
Xeverything you don't need on the next lower level, so there's
Xplenty of room for the stolen items. Drop everything you own on
Xthe pile (sell it), then pick up everything at once. You just
Xhave to wait for your autoteleport, and make it to the '>' before
Xthe shopkeeper catches up with you. Avoid the Kops as much as
Xpossible. Should you find yourself teleporting back to the shop
X(and the shopkeeper's still there), you can drop all your gold
Xbut for 1 piece, offer to pay him, and he will forget the fact
Xthat he was robbed. Just don't let him get between you and any
Xpie-throwing Kop. The wand of teleportation is a license to
Xsteal. If you dig a pit in front of a shop door or block the
Xpath with a boulder, it makes your getaway even easier.
X
XFountains and Thrones
X
XLeave these alone until your luck is maximized.
X
XPraying
X
XInvoke the 'time' option to display your move count. Pray every
X300 moves (until you get the Amulet), and you will cut your food
Xrequirement in half, double your HP's, bless every cursed ring
Xor weapon, and recover from blindness and loss of strength over
Xthe course of the game. Almost makes winning too easy.
